A||||3||FieroPerformance||Painting/Prep work questions||||1||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||08-16-2001||02:03 PM||||I am going to try to repaint my fiero while it is down for the rebuild. I was wondering if any of you have special tips or advice for preping it or painting it.<P>Right now I am using an air sander with 320 grit paper and going over it with 400 grit paper. Wet sanding.<P>Any advice would be apreciated.<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||jch82||08-16-2001||02:11 PM||||Make sure you wetsand every part of the car that is getting paint with the 400grit. When I wetsand it is always in different directions. That provides a better surface for the paint to stick. <P>I am in the process of prepping my fiero for paint too. It can be tedious work but if the prep job is bad, then the results could be deadly. Well maybe not deadly but it could end up looking really really bad....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mom and Dad they quite don't understand it<BR>ALl the kids they laugh as if they planned it<BR>Why do girls wanna pierce their nose <BR>And walk around in torn pantyhose, oh yeah<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||12
Z||000002||FieroPerformance||08-16-2001||03:34 PM||||How deep should I sand? I have been just making everything smoothed over and getting through the clear coat.<P>Should I sand all the way down through the primer everywhere?<P>-Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-16-2001||03:41 PM||||all you have to do is kill the gloss. only places you have to sand deeper are like chips and scratches. Most decent cars only need scotchbrites (Maroon ones) on most of the car. If you have any bad clear spots, you have to sand it all off to where the edges feather out. anywhere you sand thru paint or clearcoat has to be primered. most important to get edges close to moldings, rubber etc. #400 is fine to paint over. wet saves sandpaper, but doesnt get it sanded any better. I dry sand 90% myself.||||reg||1
